description: Do not mix Tailwind classes and CSS modules in the same component
alwaysApply: true
---

# CSS Modules and Tailwind

Each component uses **one** styling system. Do not mix Tailwind utility
classes with CSS module classes in the same component.

## Allowed utilities

- `sr-only`

## CSS modules only

If the component imports a `.module.css` file, every `className` must come
from that module or from the allowed utilities list.

```tsx
import styles from "./colour-picker.module.css";

<fieldset className={styles["colour-picker"]}>
  <legend className="sr-only">Available colours</legend>
</fieldset>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Tailwind layout/typography mixed with a CSS module
import styles from "./product-details.module.css";

<div className={styles["product-details"]}>
  <h1 className="text-2xl m-0">{title}</h1>
</div>
```

Move those styles into the module instead of adding Tailwind classes.

## Tailwind only

If the component does not import a CSS module, style it with Tailwind
classes only. Do not add a `.module.css` file to sprinkle a few custom
rules.

```tsx
<div className="py-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[2fr_1fr] gap-4">
```
